{"id":4209,"date":"2019-11-27T09:56:08","date_gmt":"2019-11-27T15:56:08","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/pniachg-2-2\/"},"modified":"2019-11-27T10:08:37","modified_gmt":"2019-11-27T16:08:37","slug":"pniachg-2-2","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/pniachg-2-2\/","title":{"rendered":"KING OF THE HILL III ON CBS &#038; YOUTUBE NOW"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; use_background_color_gradient=&#8221;on&#8221; background_color_gradient_start=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; background_color_gradient_end=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; custom_padding=&#8221;0px|||||&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;3.25&#8243;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;3.25&#8243; custom_padding=&#8221;|||&#8221; custom_padding__hover=&#8221;|||&#8221;][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;3px|||||&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Greetings to our amazing PNIA fans,<\/p>\n<p>Hopefully you are enjoying a shortened work week as we approach Thanksgiving here in the States. Speaking of which, the entire Poker Night crew would like to express our gratitude and thanks to our fans for your continued support over the years.<\/p>\n<p>Last night on CBS SPORTS NETWORK, the third episode of KING OF THE HILL III aired. Reruns of this episode will air Sunday night. Despite having a massive lead in the first game, Scott Blumstein was swept in the Best of 3 series versus Brandon Adams, who now awaits the winner of Dan Colman versus Olivier Busquet.<\/p>\n<p><span>If you missed the first episode of King of the Hill, it is available on YouTube for your viewing pleasure in the thumbnails below.<\/span><span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_image src=&#8221;https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/2.png&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; url=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/LbT9hvB-92g&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;][\/et_pb_image][et_pb_image src=&#8221;https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/3.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; url=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/LbT9hvB-92g&#8221; border_radii=&#8221;on|12px|12px|12px|12px&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;][\/et_pb_image][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;3px|||||&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For our fans that live in the Greater Los Angeles territories, check out our shining star, Stapes, doin\u2019 his thing at the Laugh Factory this Tuesday at 7:30pm.<\/span><\/p>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p><span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_image src=&#8221;https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/4.png&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;][\/et_pb_image][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;3px|||||&#8221;]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>It&#8217;s all gravy, no rake this Thanksgiving. Poker Night has partnered with FantasyDraft, an exciting DFS platform that has no rake! Take advantage of our new promotion by using sign up code &#8216;PNIA&#8217; and enter our free roll.<span data-stringify-type=\"paragraph-break\"><\/span>Go to\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/fantasydraft.com\/\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FantasyDraft.com<\/a>\u00a0or download the FantasyDraft app and enter the promo code \u201cPNIA\u201d for a complimentary week of rake-free daily fantasy sports.<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_image src=&#8221;https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/5.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; url=&#8221;https:\/\/www.fantasydraft.com\/&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;][\/et_pb_image][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;3px|||||&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;]<\/p>\n<div>\n<p>Enjoy the week and Happy Thanksgiving,<\/p>\n<p>Poker Night in America<\/p><\/div>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section]<\/p>\n<span class=\"et_bloom_bottom_trigger\"><\/span>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Greetings to our amazing PNIA fans, Hopefully you are enjoying a shortened work week as we approach Thanksgiving here in the States. Speaking of which, the entire Poker Night crew would like to express our gratitude and thanks to our fans for your continued support over the years. Last night on CBS SPORTS NETWORK, the [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":6,"featured_media":4213,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"gallery","meta":{"_et_pb_use_builder":"on","_et_pb_old_content":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4115\" src=\"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/2019-01-18-15_00_17-Untitled-document-Google-Docs-1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1025\" height=\"683\" \/><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">On the sad news of Gavin Smith passing, the Poker Night in America crew wanted to express a few thoughts about one of our favorite players to ever join our table. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It only took a few moments after meeting Gavin to learn a few things about him. First, you would learn immediately that he was genuine. He would tell you exactly what was on his mind, without hesitation or qualification. It\u2019s often said that every word spoken before the word \u201cbut\u201d is BS, and Gavin never used \u201cbut\u201d. He just said everything that came after, and left you to deal with it. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Which you usually could, because the next thing that became apparent in Gavin\u2019s presence was that he was hilarious. Swarthy, Canadian-accented humor rolled out of him effortlessly, and cut any tension that his candor might create. As creators of poker entertainment content, we can\u2019t overstate how great it was to have someone like Gavin at our table keeping it active and funny.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Between the lines of his jokes was a rapier wit that never seemed to dull, even in the midst of his well-known excesses. His intelligence was considerable, and seemed to be only matched by his restlessness in life. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The final thing that needs to be said is that Gavin Smith knew all the names of the members of our production crew. He may have been the only poker player that has been on our show that can claim that. He partied with us, and cracked us up, and he\u2019d ask about our lives from event to event. It seems small, but to us, it was a big deal. For that, for his candor, and his humor, he\u2019ll always have our love and respect. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/imgur.com\/a\/MCSQbqY\">Here are some of the photos<\/a> we have of Gavin from his appearances on our show. Please feel free to use these in any way you see fit in your remembrances, with no attribution required.<\/span><\/p><p>If you would like to help the Smith family, a GoFundMe account <a href=\"https:\/\/www.gofundme.com\/rip-ol039-gavin-smith\">has been created here.<\/a><\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p>","_et_gb_content_width":"","_exactmetrics_skip_tracking":f